{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WZo1GmJB9wozWsSWXkusYf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ICOLD bulletin 121 seismic analysis dams earthquake design criteria tailings 2001\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"(PDF) ICOLD's Revised Seismic Design and Performance Criteria for Large Storage Dams\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/109887424/ICOLDs_Revised_Seismic_Design_and_Performance_Criteria_for_Large_Storage_Dams\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] ICOLD s revised seismic design and performance criteria for large storage dams - Free Download PDF\",\"url\":\"https://silo.tips/download/icold-s-revised-seismic-design-and-performance-criteria-for-large-storage-dams\"},{\"title\":\"ICOLD Bulletin No. 194 TAILINGS DAM SAFETY\",\"url\":\"https://unece.org/sites/default/files/2023-04/S4-1Andy%20Small_ENG.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SELECTING SEISMIC PARAMETERS FOR LARGE DAMS Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://www.icoldchile.cl/boletines/148.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) SEISMIC DESIGN PARAMETERS FOR LARGE DAMS -ICOLD METHOD\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/307399999_SEISMIC_DESIGN_PARAMETERS_FOR_LARGE_DAMS_-ICOLD_METHOD\"},{\"title\":\"Page i COMMITTEE L TAILINGS DAMS AND WASTE LAGOONS TAILINGS DAM SAFETY\",\"url\":\"https://klohn.com/wp-content/uploads/B194-ICOLD-Tailings-Dam-Safety.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Seismic Hazard and Seismic Design and Safety Aspects of Large Dam Projects | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-07118-3_20\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Seismic Design and Performance Criteria for Large Dams and Methods of Dynamic Analysis\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/64183547/Seismic_Design_and_Performance_Criteria_for_Large_Dams_and_Methods_of_Dynamic_Analysis\"},{\"title\":\"Seismic safety evaluation of existing dams M. Wieland\",\"url\":\"https://www.cbip.org/ISRM-2022/ICOLD2021/Data/Workshop/Seismic%20Analysis%20for%20Dam%20Design%20and%20Safety%20Evaluation%20of%20Existing%20Dams/Paper%20Wieland%20seismic%20workshop%20existing%20dams%20rev%20final%202119-12-2020-16-43-44.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about ICOLD bulletins related to seismic design of dams and tailings dams, though the specific Bulletin 121 details are limited in these results.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**ICOLD Bulletin 121** is mentioned in the search results as \"Tailings Dams Risk of Dangerous Occurrences Lessons Learnt from Practical\" - it appears to be focused on tailings dam safety rather than specifically on seismic analysis and earthquake design criteria.\n\n**Related ICOLD Bulletins from around 2001:**\n- ICOLD Bulletin 120, \"Design features of dams to effectively resist seismic ground motion\" was published in 2001\n- ICOLD Bulletin 123, \"Earthquake design and evaluation of structures appurtenant to dams\" was published in 2002\n\n**Seismic Analysis and Design Criteria:**\nThe search results indicate that modern seismic design criteria were published by ICOLD in 1989 which were revised in 2010. Additionally, ICOLD publications cover topics including analysis of embankment stability during earthquakes, liquefaction potential of saturated soils during earthquakes, behaviour of tailings dams and waste disposals during seismic events.\n\nThe search results suggest that Bulletins 120 and 123 from 2001-2002 are more directly relevant to earthquake design criteria for dams than Bulletin 121, which appears to focus specifically on tailings dam risk management.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"193e9b03-f0e0-48bb-82cd-24114a1d1cbc","uuid":"fd562e20-85ec-4cc2-af63-108bc08f2367","timestamp":"2026-07-06T19:44:15.323Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ICOLD bulletin 121 seismic analysis dams earthquake design criteria tailings 2001","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015cbSHacRZguXhXzN1pPExX","content":[{"title":"(PDF) ICOLD's Revised Seismic Design and Performance Criteria for Large Storage Dams","url":"https://www.academia.edu/109887424/ICOLDs_Revised_Seismic_Design_and_Performance_Criteria_for_Large_Storage_Dams"},{"title":"[PDF] ICOLD s revised seismic design and performance criteria for large storage dams - Free Download PDF","url":"https://silo.tips/download/icold-s-revised-seismic-design-and-performance-criteria-for-large-storage-dams"},{"title":"ICOLD Bulletin No. 194 TAILINGS DAM SAFETY","url":"https://unece.org/sites/default/files/2023-04/S4-1Andy%20Small_ENG.pdf"},{"title":"SELECTING SEISMIC PARAMETERS FOR LARGE DAMS Guidelines","url":"https://www.icoldchile.cl/boletines/148.pdf"},{"title":"(PDF) SEISMIC DESIGN PARAMETERS FOR LARGE DAMS -ICOLD METHOD","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/307399999_SEISMIC_DESIGN_PARAMETERS_FOR_LARGE_DAMS_-ICOLD_METHOD"},{"title":"Page i COMMITTEE L TAILINGS DAMS AND WASTE LAGOONS TAILINGS DAM SAFETY","url":"https://klohn.com/wp-content/uploads/B194-ICOLD-Tailings-Dam-Safety.pdf"},{"title":"Seismic Hazard and Seismic Design and Safety Aspects of Large Dam Projects | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-07118-3_20"},{"title":"(PDF) Seismic Design and Performance Criteria for Large Dams and Methods of Dynamic Analysis","url":"https://www.academia.edu/64183547/Seismic_Design_and_Performance_Criteria_for_Large_Dams_and_Methods_of_Dynamic_Analysis"},{"title":"Seismic safety evaluation of existing dams M. Wieland","url":"https://www.cbip.org/ISRM-2022/ICOLD2021/Data/Workshop/Seismic%20Analysis%20for%20Dam%20Design%20and%20Safety%20Evaluation%20of%20Existing%20Dams/Paper%20Wieland%20seismic%20workshop%20existing%20dams%20rev%20final%202119-12-2020-16-43-44.pdf"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about ICOLD bulletins related to seismic design of dams and tailings dams, though the specific Bulletin 121 details are limited in these results.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**ICOLD Bulletin 121** is mentioned in the search results as \"Tailings Dams Risk of Dangerous Occurrences Lessons Learnt from Practical\" - it appears to be focused on tailings dam safety rather than specifically on seismic analysis and earthquake design criteria.\n\n**Related ICOLD Bulletins from around 2001:**\n- ICOLD Bulletin 120, \"Design features of dams to effectively resist seismic ground motion\" was published in 2001\n- ICOLD Bulletin 123, \"Earthquake design and evaluation of structures appurtenant to dams\" was published in 2002\n\n**Seismic Analysis and Design Criteria:**\nThe search results indicate that modern seismic design criteria were published by ICOLD in 1989 which were revised in 2010. Additionally, ICOLD publications cover topics including analysis of embankment stability during earthquakes, liquefaction potential of saturated soils during earthquakes, behaviour of tailings dams and waste disposals during seismic events.\n\nThe search results suggest that Bulletins 120 and 123 from 2001-2002 are more directly relevant to earthquake design criteria for dams than Bulletin 121, which appears to focus specifically on tailings dam risk management."],"durationSeconds":7.20877883299999,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019k49RWQbJzS91CjmsFqkxT","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Idriss Boulanger 2008 soil liquefaction earthquakes CPT SPT triggering criteria tailings\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CPT AND SPT BASED LIQUEFACTION TRIGGERING ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.ce.memphis.edu/7137/PDFs/Notes/i3Boulanger_Idriss_CPT_and_SPT_Liq_triggering_CGM-14-01_20141.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SOIL-LIQUEFACTION-DURING-EARTHQUAKES - Idriss Boulanger 2008 Book PDF | PDF | Soil Mechanics | Nature\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/338142211/SOIL-LIQUEFACTION-DURING-EARTHQUAKES-Idriss-Boulanger-2008-book-pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SPT-BASED LIQUEFACTION TRIGGERING PROCEDURES\",\"url\":\"https://faculty.engineering.ucdavis.edu/boulanger/wp-content/uploads/sites/71/2014/09/Idriss_Boulanger_SPT_Liquefaction_CGM-10-02.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"2008 EERI Monograph \\\"Soil Liquifaction During ...\",\"url\":\"https://vulcanhammer.net/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/liquefactionreview.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CENTER FOR GEOTECHNICAL MODELING REPORT NO. UCD/CGM-14/01 CPT AND SPT BASED\",\"url\":\"https://faculty.engineering.ucdavis.edu/boulanger/wp-content/uploads/sites/71/2014/09/Boulanger_Idriss_CPT_and_SPT_Liq_triggering_CGM-14-01_20141.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) SPT-Based probabilistic and deterministic assessment of seismic soil liquefaction initiation hazard\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/32892111/SPT_Based_probabilistic_and_deterministic_assessment_of_seismic_soil_liquefaction_initiation_hazard\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Soil Liquefaction During Earthquakes M. Idriss and Ross W. Boulanger\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/144513615/Soil_Liquefaction_During_Earthquakes_M_Idriss_and_Ross_W_Boulanger\"},{\"title\":\"Soil liquefaction during earthquakes | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/288624104_Soil_liquefaction_during_earthquakes\"}]\n\nI've found search results related to your query. Here's what the search returned:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\nThe 2008 EERI Monograph on \"Soil Liquefaction During Earthquakes\" by Idriss and Boulanger (2008) is a significant work in this field. \n\nThe framework described in Idriss and Boulanger (2008) was later updated with a revised magnitude scaling factor (MSF) that accounts for the effects of soil type and denseness.\n\nThe Idriss and Boulanger (2008) procedures are among two analytical frameworks widely accepted by the industry. A significant achievement of these new procedures is their new criteria for assessment of liquefaction potential of low-plasticity silts and clays.\n\nThe search results include references to both CPT (Cone Penetration Test) and SPT (Standard Penetration Test) based liquefaction triggering methods from this 2008 work. Idriss and Boulanger (2008) summarized residual strength relationships based on penetration resistance correlations, indicating that liquefied strength ratios for highly contractive soils may approach values on the order of 0.01-0.03 at low normalized resistance levels.\n\nThe search also referenced liquefaction failure of tailings dams resulting from the Near Izu Oshima earthquake in academic literature on this topic.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"193e9b03-f0e0-48bb-82cd-24114a1d1cbc","uuid":"6ae6856f-a85c-47b8-bf94-26fe238c9424","timestamp":"2026-07-06T19:44:18.264Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Idriss Boulanger 2008 soil liquefaction earthquakes CPT SPT triggering criteria tailings","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018vo186Efquv8si9osHkb2H","content":[{"title":"CPT AND SPT BASED LIQUEFACTION TRIGGERING ...","url":"http://www.ce.memphis.edu/7137/PDFs/Notes/i3Boulanger_Idriss_CPT_and_SPT_Liq_triggering_CGM-14-01_20141.pdf"},{"title":"SOIL-LIQUEFACTION-DURING-EARTHQUAKES - Idriss Boulanger 2008 Book PDF | PDF | Soil Mechanics | Nature","url":"https://www.scribd.com/document/338142211/SOIL-LIQUEFACTION-DURING-EARTHQUAKES-Idriss-Boulanger-2008-book-pdf"},{"title":"SPT-BASED LIQUEFACTION TRIGGERING PROCEDURES","url":"https://faculty.engineering.ucdavis.edu/boulanger/wp-content/uploads/sites/71/2014/09/Idriss_Boulanger_SPT_Liquefaction_CGM-10-02.pdf"},{"title":"2008 EERI Monograph \"Soil Liquifaction During ...","url":"https://vulcanhammer.net/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/liquefactionreview.pdf"},{"title":"CENTER FOR GEOTECHNICAL MODELING REPORT NO. UCD/CGM-14/01 CPT AND SPT BASED","url":"https://faculty.engineering.ucdavis.edu/boulanger/wp-content/uploads/sites/71/2014/09/Boulanger_Idriss_CPT_and_SPT_Liq_triggering_CGM-14-01_20141.pdf"},{"title":"(PDF) SPT-Based probabilistic and deterministic assessment of seismic soil liquefaction initiation hazard","url":"https://www.academia.edu/32892111/SPT_Based_probabilistic_and_deterministic_assessment_of_seismic_soil_liquefaction_initiation_hazard"},{"title":"(PDF) Soil Liquefaction During Earthquakes M. Idriss and Ross W. Boulanger","url":"https://www.academia.edu/144513615/Soil_Liquefaction_During_Earthquakes_M_Idriss_and_Ross_W_Boulanger"},{"title":"Soil liquefaction during earthquakes | Request PDF","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/288624104_Soil_liquefaction_during_earthquakes"}]},"I've found search results related to your query. Here's what the search returned:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\nThe 2008 EERI Monograph on \"Soil Liquefaction During Earthquakes\" by Idriss and Boulanger (2008) is a significant work in this field. \n\nThe framework described in Idriss and Boulanger (2008) was later updated with a revised magnitude scaling factor (MSF) that accounts for the effects of soil type and denseness.\n\nThe Idriss and Boulanger (2008) procedures are among two analytical frameworks widely accepted by the industry. A significant achievement of these new procedures is their new criteria for assessment of liquefaction potential of low-plasticity silts and clays.\n\nThe search results include references to both CPT (Cone Penetration Test) and SPT (Standard Penetration Test) based liquefaction triggering methods from this 2008 work. Idriss and Boulanger (2008) summarized residual strength relationships based on penetration resistance correlations, indicating that liquefied strength ratios for highly contractive soils may approach values on the order of 0.01-0.03 at low normalized resistance levels.\n\nThe search also referenced liquefaction failure of tailings dams resulting from the Near Izu Oshima earthquake in academic literature on this topic."],"durationSeconds":9.190909333000018,"searchCount":1}}
